The Meta Principle

The highest-leverage communicator is not the best storyteller.

Nor the best mathematician.

Nor the best engineer.

It is the one who can choose the appropriate compiler for the current audience, objective, and constraints.

The medium is selected by the mission.

The mission is not constrained by the medium.

⸻

Final Compression

Every form of communication is a compiler.

Every compiler preserves some invariants and discards others.

Mastery is not speaking one language fluently.

Mastery is translating one invariant faithfully across many languages while knowing what each gains, what each loses, and when each should be used.